- A reasonable amount of reading matter for the flight;
- infant's food for consumption in flight;
- A small amount of duty-free goods

Please ensure your bags that you pack with your luggage are of a suitable type and of sound construction to protect its content. Naoero Airlines is not responsible for repair or replacement of bags that are presented at check-in that are not adequate or suitable to protect the contents from damage.

For International Travel on Naoero Airlines flights the following baggage allowances are included in your Fare. All other Baggage which is larger and/or heavier than your allowance will constitute excess and/or oversized Baggage. Pooling of baggage is only permitted where passengers are part of a family group and have been booked on the same booking reference number (PNR). Fees are payable for any excess baggage and must be paid for at the time of check-in.

Naoero Airlines does not accept the following items as Checked Baggage and does not accept liability for their loss or damage unless the items are identified to Naoero Airlines and it has, in its absolute discretion, given its written acceptance for carriage and accepted liability in writing for their loss or damage:
- Cash, credit cards, deeds, passports and other travel documents, securities, business documents or other valuable documents;
- Jewellery, antiques, precious metals or similar valuable items;
- Any item of a delicate, fragile or brittle nature e.g. glassware, sports equipment, musical instruments;
- Any item of a perishable nature e.g. seafood;
- Medicines;
- Electrical or electronic components e.g. computers, cameras;
- Any item that has insufficient packaging to withstand the normal circumstances and effects of carriage by air.

The following baggage related claims are not covered by Naoero Airlines:
- scratches, dents or minor cuts to pieces of baggage
- damage to or loss of straps, hooks or belts
- broken wheels or feet
- damage to zips or locks
- damage to retractable or fixed baggage handles
- damage as a result of over-packing.
